# Hand axe at microcube resolution (1 microcube = 1/9 unit).
# Handtools are held in the fist, so they MUST be authored in microcubes and
# stay skinny (1 microcube thick) — full cubes are far too coarse (see the
# longsword sword_fine.voxel for the reference convention).
# Origin at handle base, extends up (+Y); the single-bit head flares to +X.
# Grip column sits at X=4, Z=4 (same as sword_fine) so the item's held
# gripOffset matches the sword. Total ~1.2 units tall.
# M px py pz  sx sy sz  mx my mz  Material

# --- Handle (Wood), X=4 Z=4, Y=0..10 (skinny, 1 microcube thick) ---
M 0 0 0 1 0 1 1 0 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 0 1 1 1 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 0 1 1 2 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 1 1 1 0 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 1 1 1 1 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 1 1 1 2 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 2 1 1 0 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 2 1 1 1 1 Wood
M 0 0 0 1 2 1 1 2 1 Wood
M 0 1 0 1 0 1 1 0 1 Wood
M 0 1 0 1 0 1 1 1 1 Wood

# --- Head poll (Metal), small nub behind the handle, X=3 Y=8 ---
M 0 0 0 1 2 1 0 2 1 Metal

# --- Bit / blade (Metal), flares out +X and curves down, edge at X=7 ---
# Y=5  X=5,6
M 0 0 0 1 1 1 2 2 1 Metal
M 0 0 0 2 1 1 0 2 1 Metal
# Y=6  X=5,6,7
M 0 0 0 1 2 1 2 0 1 Metal
M 0 0 0 2 2 1 0 0 1 Metal
M 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 0 1 Metal
# Y=7  X=5,6,7
M 0 0 0 1 2 1 2 1 1 Metal
M 0 0 0 2 2 1 0 1 1 Metal
M 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 1 1 Metal
# Y=8  X=5,6,7
M 0 0 0 1 2 1 2 2 1 Metal
M 0 0 0 2 2 1 0 2 1 Metal
M 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 2 1 Metal
# Y=9  X=5,6
M 0 1 0 1 0 1 2 0 1 Metal
M 0 1 0 2 0 1 0 0 1 Metal
